      "sequence_position": 7,
      "problem": "Given an arithmetic sequence that has ${a}_{8}=8$ and the common difference $d=4$, what is the general formula for the $n$th term of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "Since ${a}_{8}=8$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we can determine the first term of the sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ 8 & ={a}_{1}+7(4) \\\\ 8 & ={a}_{1}+28 \\\\ -20 & ={a}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-20+(n-1)(4) \\\\  & =-20+4n-4 \\\\  & =4n-24\\end{aligned}\n$$",
